.\" Manual page for segler, the command-line tool.
.\"
.\" The tool answers --help for itself and for every subcommand, and that is
.\" the authority on its arguments; this page is the summary lintian wants in
.\" every package that installs a binary, and it says where to look rather
.\" than restating every option.
.\"
.\" Author: David M. Anderson
.\" Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
.TH SEGLER 1 "2026\-09\-04" "segler @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
segler \- tools for DocLang documents and archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B segler
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I file
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B segler
is the command\-line tool over the library that
.BR segler\-desktop (1)
is built on. It reads a
.I .dclg
document or a
.I .dclx
archive and reports on it, validates it, prints what the window would draw,
or applies edits to it and writes the result.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "inspect " file
Report what a document or archive contains: the version, the page count, the
element counts, and for an archive the page images and assets.
.TP
.BI "validate " file
Check a document against the DocLang schema and rules. Each finding names the
layer, the rule, the element's path and the reason. Exits non\-zero on any
finding.
.TP
.BI "page " file " " [ number ]
Show one page as the window draws it: its located boxes and its tree.
.TP
.BI "render " file " " [ number ]
Print one page as the blocks the document pane draws.
.TP
.BI "table " file " " path
Print a table's grid: each cell with its kind, span and text.
.TP
.BI "edit " "\-e edit ... " file " " [ "\-o out" ] " " [ \-\-undo ]
Apply edits through the same session the window uses and write the result to
.I out
or to the standard output. With
.B \-\-undo
every edit is undone afterwards and the document is checked against what was
opened, byte for byte. The edits and their paths are described by
.BR "segler edit \-\-help" .
.TP
.BI "corpus " directory " " [ \-\-toolkit ]
Round\-trip and validate every DocLang file under a directory, meant for a
checkout of the specification repository: files under a
.I valid
directory must produce no findings and files under
.I invalid
at least one. With
.B \-\-toolkit
the reference toolkit's verdict is compared against this one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help for the tool or for a command.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when the command succeeded and, for
.BR validate ,
.B edit \-\-undo
and
.BR corpus ,
when nothing was found; non\-zero otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR segler\-desktop (1)
.PP
The format is specified in spec.md in the DocLang repository at
https://github.com/doclang\-project/doclang.
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson
